//  count and a 14-node continuous posterior. It narrates its perception
//  through alerts and reports. It does not place orders. It does not have
//  independent agency. It is a decision-support agent — an intelligence
//  layer between you and the market.
//
//  I built this for myself. I wanted a way to read the market not as a
//  series of signals to react to, but as a set of observable states that
//  could be read, understood, and reasoned about. Every layer in this
//  script answers a question that the previous layer raised.
//
//  The result is not a prediction engine. It is a spatial and contextual
//  framework — a way of organizing price information so that structure,
//  direction, momentum, volatility, and session context are all visible at
//  once, without one hiding behind another.
//
//  This is not artificial intelligence. It is not machine learning. It is
//  not a trained model. It is a deterministic, transparent, rule-based
//  system that applies established market concepts (ICT, SMC, Hull, RSI,
//  ATR, Fibonacci) through a weighted fusion architecture — and shows you
//  every step of the reasoning.
//
//  The word "neural" appears in the interface as a descriptive label for
//  the weighted fusion layer, not a reference to neural networks.
//
//  I am publishing it open-source because I think this way of seeing is
//  worth sharing. If you use it and find something in it, tell me. That
//  is the only thing I am asking for.
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  BUILT FOR GMT+3
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  Most trading tools are built for New York or London. They render killzones
//  at 3 AM Nairobi time, format timestamps in EST, and assume the trader is
//  awake when the Western session opens.
//
//  This script was built the other way around. The default timezone is GMT+3
//  (East Africa Time). Every session block — Asia, London, NY AM, LDN-NY,
//  NY PM — is tuned so that the label on the chart matches the clock on the
//  wall of a trader in Nairobi, Kampala, Dar es Salaam, Addis Ababa, Cairo,
//  Riyadh, or Moscow.
//
//  The session blocks are ICT-inspired, not literal ICT killzone boundaries.
//  They were chosen because they cover the trading day a GMT+3 trader actually
//  sees — from the Asian open to the New York close — without forcing them to
//  mentally translate time zones every time they look at the chart.
//
//  Every timestamp in the script — HUD, tooltips, analysis report, episodic
//  memory — renders in GMT+3. If you trade from a different zone, the timezone
//  selector lets you change it. But the default was chosen deliberately.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE TOOLTIPS ARE A COMPLETE TRADING PLAN
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  Most indicators give you a label. Hover it, and you get a name. Maybe a
//  number. That is all.
//
//  This script gives you a plan. Every signal label, every zone label, and
//  every entry label carries a tooltip that contains everything you need to
//  place and manage the trade — without opening a single additional panel.
//
//  SIGNAL TOOLTIP — the trade thesis:
//      • Direction and score (x/8)
//      • Execution mode and product (Signal / Multipliers / Vanilla)
//      • Contract direction, multiplier, risk sizing
//      • Stop loss price, distance in points and ticks
//      • TP1 / TP2 / TP3 prices with R multiples
//      • Fib regime source, HTF timeframe, LTF and HTF states, bars since flip
//      • Gate pass/block status for both directions
//      • Posterior probabilities, probability edge, zone confidence
//      • Node-by-node reasoning — every confluence node with ✓ or ✗
//      • Active killzone, timestamp in GMT+3, chart link
//
//  ENTRY TOOLTIP — the execution slip:
//      • Direction (CALL / PUT / LONG / SHORT) and execution mode
//      • Score and posterior
//      • Entry mode and entry price
//      • Stop loss with distance
//      • TP1 / TP2 / TP3 with distance for each
//      • Strike and expiry (options) or contract and multiplier (multipliers)
//
//  ZONE TOOLTIP — the spatial brief:
//      • Zone direction and event type
//      • High, low, and range
//      • Trail state and Ultron Gate state
//      • LTF Fib and HTF Fib regime
//      • Gate agreement status
//      • Zone confidence and posterior probabilities
//
//  The intent is that a trader never has to look anywhere else. The chart
//  tells you what is happening. The tooltip tells you what to do about it,
//  and why. Whether you take the trade is still your decision — but the
//  information is all in one place, on the hover.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CONCEPTS, ATTRIBUTION & ORIGINALITY
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  ULTRON Alpha is an integrated market-analysis implementation developed to
//  organize multiple dimensions of price information into a unified spatial
//  and contextual framework.
//
//  The system incorporates established market-analysis concepts together with
//  original integration, state handling, filtering, visual interpretation,
//  event processing, and analytical presentation developed by the author.
//
//
//  CONCEPT & METHOD ATTRIBUTION
//  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//  • ICT / Inner Circle Trader concepts
//      Market-structure terminology, killzones, liquidity concepts, BOS/CHoCH,
//      order-block concepts, fair-value-gap concepts, premium/discount
//      concepts, liquidity sweeps, and related price-action terminology.
//      Session windows are ICT-inspired but tuned to GMT+3 (East Africa
//      Time), not literal ICT killzone boundaries. See "BUILT FOR GMT+3".
//
//  • Smart Money Concepts (SMC) — LuxAlgo
//      The SMC structural layer in this script (swing/internal pivots,
//      BOS/CHoCH detection, order-block storage and mitigation,
//      fair-value-gap rendering, premium/equilibrium/discount zone
//      projection, strong/weak high/low labelling, and equal high/low
//      detection) is adapted from the publicly available "Smart Money
//      Concepts (SMC) [LuxAlgo]" indicator. The original work is credited
//      to LuxAlgo. Any bugs or behavioural differences in this adaptation
//      are the responsibility of the author of this script, not LuxAlgo.
//
//  • Hull Moving Average — Alan Hull
//      The HMA/EHMA/THMA Hull Suite implementation follows the classic Hull
//      Moving Average formulation associated with Alan Hull. The wrapper
//      pattern is a standard public implementation.
//
//  • RSI / ATR — J. Welles Wilder
//      Classic Relative Strength Index and Average True Range methodologies
//      associated with J. Welles Wilder, used in momentum, volatility,
//      trail, and strike-distance calculations.
//
//  • Fibonacci retracement and extension levels
//      Standard 0.382 / 0.5 / 0.618 / 0.786 retracement and 1.272 / 1.414 /
//      1.618 / 2.0 / 2.618 extension ratios. These are mathematical
//      constants, not proprietary formulas.
//
//  • Multiplier-contract asset-class mapping
//      Asset-class detection (crypto_major, crypto_minor, commodity_metal,
//      commodity_oil, synthetic_vol, synthetic_jump, synthetic_bullbear,
//      forex) and multiplier-cap tiers reflect publicly documented contract
//      limits for multiplier-style derivative products. Caps change over
//      time; users should verify current limits with their own broker.
//
//  These references identify conceptual and methodological foundations.
//  They do not imply endorsement, sponsorship, partnership, or affiliation
//  with any third-party educator, author, organization, or vendor unless
//  expressly stated.
//
//
//  ORIGINALITY & OPEN-SOURCE IMPLEMENTATION
//  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  ULTRON Alpha is not presented as a new invention of the underlying market
//  concepts themselves. Its original character resides in the implementation
//  and integration of those concepts into a unified analytical framework.
//
//  The distinctive implementation includes original combinations of:
//
//      • Three-tier architecture (Observation / Judgement / Execution)
//      • Speculative Probabilistic Core — a 14-node continuous fusion
//        layer with configurable weights and sigmoid temperature
//      • Zone Confidence Engine — multi-source corroboration scoring for
//        CHoCH zones with star grading (⭐ / ⭐⭐ / ⭐⭐⭐)
//      • HTF Fibonacci Projection — regime-anchored retracement and
//        extension grid redrawn at barstate.islast
//      • Zone Quality Gate — width / HTF-agreement / extension guards that
//        filter CHoCH zones before they become tradeable
//      • Consolidated Alert Dispatcher — priority-queue alert logic
//        (trade events > triggers > informational > blocked observations >
//        scale-ins) ensuring at most one message per bar
//      • Episodic Memory — a rolling event buffer with session tagging,
//        rendered in the analysis report
//      • Synthetic-aware node weighting — discounts fake volume on
//        synthetic instruments
//      • Broker-aware execution engine — asset-class detection, multiplier
//        caps, contract-direction mapping, deal-cancellation availability,
//        and strike selection (ATM/ITM/OTM/Dynamic) for vanilla options
//      • Tooltip-as-trading-plan — every signal, entry, and zone label
//        carries a full trade thesis on hover
//
//  The exact formulas, thresholds, weighting relationships, state
//  transitions, internal calculations, decision sequencing, and
//  event-processing mechanisms are visible in the open source. You are
//  encouraged to read them.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  WHAT THIS INDICATOR IS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  ULTRON Alpha is a multi-timeframe market-analysis engine designed to help
//  organize price action into observable structural, directional, spatial,
//  momentum, volatility, and session-based states.
//
//  Depending on configuration, the indicator can provide:
//
//      • Internal and swing market-structure information
//      • BOS / CHoCH structural references
//      • Liquidity and price-location zones
//      • Fibonacci-based spatial references (LTF + HTF projection)
//      • Trend-regime context (Macro Hull, Fast Hull, Trail)
//      • Adaptive price trails with an Alpha Gate permission layer
//      • Momentum and confluence states (8-node discrete score)
//      • A speculative fusion layer (14-node continuous probability)
//      • Zone confidence grading (⭐ / ⭐⭐ / ⭐⭐⭐)
//      • Session / killzone context tuned to GMT+3
//      • Visual entry, stop and target planning references
//      • Position lifecycle management (entry → TP1 → TP2 → TP3 → exit)
//      • A dashboard summarizing multiple analytical states
//      • Configurable alert and event outputs (consolidated,
//        verbosity-controlled, with optional raw JSON payloads)
//
//  The indicator is intended to organize information rather than remove
//  the need for human judgment.
//
//  IMPORTANT — ON THE WORD "NEURAL":
//  The terms "Neural", "Neural Confluence", and "Speculative Probabilistic
//  Core" are descriptive labels for a weighted fusion layer composed of
//  bounded node outputs and sigmoid transformations. This script does not
//  use machine learning, neural networks, deep learning, or any trained
//  model. The fusion is deterministic, transparent, and fully auditable.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CORE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  ULTRON follows the principle:
//
//      READ PRICE → BUILD CONTEXT → OBSERVE → PLAN → EXECUTE
//
//  The system is designed around the idea that market intelligence should
//  be observable, structured, explainable at the output level, and usable
//  as part of a broader discretionary or systematic workflow.
//
//  ULTRON does not guarantee future market direction, signal accuracy,
//  profitability, or any particular trading outcome.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ANALYTICAL ARCHITECTURE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  At a high level, ULTRON Alpha is organized around a three-tier
//  architecture:
//
//      Tier 1 · OBSERVATION
//          Everything is drawn, unconditionally. Structure, zones, Fibs,
//          killzones, liquidity, Hull bands, trail — all visible regardless
//          of score. Nothing is hidden behind a gate.
//
//      Tier 2 · JUDGEMENT
//          8-node discrete confluence score + quality gates + Fib regime.
//          This layer answers "is this structurally sound?" with a count.
//          Transparent, auditable, and manually tunable.
//
//      Tier 2.5 · SPECULATION
//          14-node continuous fusion layer. Each node outputs a bounded
//          value, not a yes/no. Weights are configurable. This layer
//          answers "how much conviction?" and runs in parallel with Tier 2.
//
//      Tier 3 · EXECUTION
//          Position Tool fires only when Tier 2 clears. Entry mode
//          (Signal Change / Trail Retest / Zone Retest), TP ladder,
//          breakeven logic, and trail-flip exits are all managed here.
//
//  The exact internal relationships between these layers are visible in
//  the open source. The output — HUD, zone labels, tooltips, alerts — is
//  explainable at the output level.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  MULTI-TIMEFRAME USE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  ULTRON can be configured for different chart timeframes and market
//  contexts. Higher-timeframe information is used for regime context (HTF
//  Fib gate, MTF CHoCH confluence, HTF Swing Projection), while
//  lower-timeframe information drives tactical triggers.
//
//  Multiple request.security calls are used: one for the HTF Fib regime
//  (with [1] for confirmed-bar integrity), one for MTF CHoCH confluence,
//  and one for HTF Fib Swing Projection. All use lookahead_off. No
//  lookahead bias is introduced.
//
//  Users should evaluate the behavior of the indicator on the instruments
//  and timeframes for which they intend to use it. Recommended use is on
//  liquid markets where underlying structure is not dominated by gaps or
//  synthetic noise.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  POSITION & TRADE-PLANNING TOOLS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  The indicator includes visual position-planning functionality that can
//  display entry references, stop references, target references, and
//  evolving trade-management states.
//
//  Three entry modes are supported:
//      • Signal Change — enter on trail flip
//      • Trail Retest — wait for price to retest the trail after a flip
//      • Zone Retest — wait for price to retrace into the active CHoCH zone
//
//  These elements are analytical and visual tools. They do not represent
//  an execution instruction, brokerage order, or guarantee that a market
//  level will be reached.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  EXECUTION ENGINE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  The execution engine is broker-agnostic but includes logic for
//  multiplier-contract environments (asset-class caps, contract-direction
//  mapping, deal-cancellation availability) and vanilla-options environments
//  (strike selection, suggested expiry).
//
//  Three execution modes are supported:
//      • Signal Only — no execution context, labels only
//      • Multipliers — multiplier-style contracts with asset-class caps
//        and risk-per-trade sizing
//      • Vanilla Options — CALL/PUT strike selection (ATM/ITM/OTM/Dynamic)
//        with suggested expiry
//
//  Multiplier caps are display-only and reflect publicly documented limits
//  for multiplier-style derivative products. They are not a guarantee of
//  what your broker will accept.
//
//  This is not financial advice. No execution is performed by this script.
//  The script does not place orders. It produces visual references and
//  alert payloads. You are responsible for every trade you take.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ALERTS & EVENT PROCESSING
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  ULTRON includes configurable alert conditions and event-driven outputs.
//
//  The consolidated dispatcher uses a priority queue:
//      1. Trade events (entry, TP1, TP2, TP3, exit)
//      2. Trigger signals
//      3. Informational (score context, blocked observations)
//      4. Scale-ins and regime exits
//
//  At most ONE message per bar is sent. Trade events take priority over
//  informational messages. The Alert Verbosity selector (All / Consolidated
//  / Trade Events Only) controls how much chatter reaches your webhook.
//
//  Raw JSON payloads are OFF by default. Turn them ON only if you have an
//  external webhook consumer. This prevents duplicate JSON payloads from
//  reaching a messaging endpoint.
//
//  Alert behavior depends on the user's selected settings, chart timeframe,
//  symbol, market data, and TradingView alert configuration.
//
//  Alert outputs should be treated as informational events generated from
//  the indicator's current analytical state.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  LIMITATIONS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  • This is an INDICATOR, not a STRATEGY. There is no strategy() call,
//    no backtest, no Strategy Tester results, no Performance Report. Any
//    claim of backtested performance is invalid.
//
//  • Repaint surface: the current bar's trail flip, CHoCH break, and
//    close-based scoring can change until the bar closes. HTF Fib
//    Projection redraws at barstate.islast. Alerts and gates use
//    barstate.isconfirmed, so the signal does not repaint — but the
//    drawing does.
//
//  • Compute weight: this script is heavy. Use "Calc Only Last N Bars"
//    and "Show Last N Zones" on high-timeframe or long-history charts.
//    Drawing budget is 500 labels / 500 boxes / 500 lines each, managed
//    by an active-set / stored-set recycling system. Exceeding the budget
//    will cause older drawings to be deleted.
//
//  • "Neural" is a naming choice, not machine learning. The fusion layer
//    is weighted sigmoid combination of bounded node outputs. It is
//    transparent, auditable, and configurable. It is not a trained model.
//
//  • Market conditions can change rapidly and may invalidate previous
//    context.
//
//  • Technical indicators operate on historical and current market data
//    and cannot know future prices.
//
//  • Different instruments and timeframes can produce materially different
//    behavior.
//
//  • Indicator calculations may be affected by the availability and
//    quality of the underlying market data. Synthetic instruments may
//    carry volume data that is not meaningful; the synthetic-aware weight
//    zeroing handles this in the fusion layer, but not in the 8-node
//    discrete score.
//
//  • Visual states and alerts should be independently evaluated before
//    use.
//
//  • No analytical system can eliminate market risk or guarantee results.
//
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  DISCLAIMER
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
